Changes in v6:
- retarget free-by-presence comment and v5 Changes sentence to
  later resize; alloc_buffer_pool() already undoes partials on this
  open-fail path (free-by-presence policy unchanged)
- debug fmt %u for unsigned num_rx_queues in
  alloc/free_buffer_pools
- pool helper unwind no longer consumes open-path i, so TX LTB
  fall-through free works on pool-fail (pre-existing shared-i leak);
  not a standalone Fixes: tag; P06 gives TX its own unwind
- post-register pool-fail without h_free_logical_lan predates this
  helper patch (inline pool loop fell through the same way). Series tip
  fixes ordering in P06 (h_free before pool DMA on open-fail via
  out_unregister_lan) and P07 (pools before register_rx_queues;
  post-register errors funnel through free_all_queues). No further change
  on P04.

Changes in v5:
- vs mailed v4: keep pool_active[] = {1,1,0,0,1} (v4 set the 64 KiB
  pool inactive). No code delta vs prior patches here; SQ large-receive /
  CMO stay at the historical baseline. change_mtu does not re-enable
  pool4 at MTU 1500; MQ memory pressure belongs at scale-up, not SQ
  default
- Unwind / free pools by real allocations (free_map/dma_addr/skbuff),
  not only pool->active (needed on later resize; a pool can still
  hold memory after active is cleared). alloc_buffer_pool() already
  undoes its own partials on this open-fail path
- Clarify kdoc: free paths use allocation presence (not "all active");
  queue 1..N metadata copy from queue 0 (v4 said "queues 1-15" while
  MAX is still 1 here)
- Document poolN sysfs size multiplies by num_rx_queues (queue 0 is the
  shared template; no per-queue pool sysfs in this series)
- Call out close() pool-free before cleanup_rx_resources, after LAN/
  NAPI/IRQ teardown (order already in v4; spell it for later drain)

Changes in v4:
- Introduce the pool helpers in the same patch that wires their first
